<h1>Questions and answers</h1>

<section class="faq">

<h2 id="what">What is RoomXDynamics?</h2>
<p>RoomXDynamics is an iPhone app in development. It simulates a slice through a room with an outside wall and a window. It shows, qualitatively, how warm and cool air move in the model, how cool the wall surface gets and how the window shifts the felt-temperature trend.</p>

<h2 id="available">Can I download it?</h2>
<p>Not yet. RoomXDynamics is in development and not yet available in the App Store. You can join the <a href="/waitlist/">waitlist</a> by email.</p>

<h2 id="results">What do the results show?</h2>
<p>Trends in the model, not values for your room. The air movement is a simplified two-dimensional picture. The wall surface temperature is calculated with simple, common assumptions (steady-state heat conduction with common design values, not checked against standard texts). The results have not been checked against real rooms. The <a href="/method/">method</a> page lists what the model leaves out.</p>

<h2 id="measure">Does the app take measurements?</h2>
<p>No. RoomXDynamics calculates from the inputs you choose, such as outside temperature, window and wall. It does not replace an on-site measurement or an expert report.</p>

<h2 id="mould">Does it tell me whether a wall will get mould?</h2>
<p>No. The wall view, which is in development, shows a qualitative risk estimate for the wall surface in three levels, with a range. It shows where the wall gets critically cool in the model. It does not say whether mould will grow on a real wall, or why. If you can see mould, consult a qualified building surveyor.</p>

<h2 id="price">Is there a price yet?</h2>
<p>The price has not been set. The waitlist is non-binding: no pre-order and no payment.</p>

<h2 id="privacy">Does this website track me?</h2>
<p>No. This website has no cookies, no analytics and no tracking. Details are in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>

<h2 id="audience">Who is it for?</h2>
<p>People who furnish, renovate or design their home and want to see, in a simple model, how warm and cool air moves in a room and how cool its walls get. It shows a model room, not a copy of yours.</p>

</section>
